# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Komback — Apache config for the cPanel / Phusion Passenger deployment.
#
# THIS IS A TEMPLATE. Copy it to your server, fill in the YOURUSER / version
# values, and save it as `.htaccess`. Do not commit it back with real paths.
#
# WHERE IT GOES — the DOCUMENT ROOT of the domain (what cPanel lists as the
# domain's "Document Root"), which must be the SAME folder as the Node app's
# "Application root" (the folder containing app.js, dist/ and node_modules/).
#
#   /home/YOURUSER/KombackWeb   <-- app root AND document root
#
# If they are different folders, Apache never reads this file for the domain,
# Passenger never hands a request to Node, and the domain is served as plain
# static files: the SPA loads, then every /api/* call comes back as HTML and the
# UI reports `Cannot read properties of null (reading 'categories')`.
#
# TWO RULES
#   1. Keep the Passenger block below (cPanel's "Setup Node.js App" normally
#      writes it for you — if it is already there, leave it untouched).
#   2. There must be NO catch-all rewrite to /index.html and NO
#      `FallbackResource`. server/index.ts already serves index.html for every
#      non-API route and substitutes the SEO tokens (%SEO_TITLE% etc.) first.
#      A catch-all hijacks /api/*, /robots.txt, /sitemap.xml and /llms.txt, and
#      ships the raw, unsubstituted template to browsers and crawlers.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# DO NOT REMOVE. CLOUDLINUX PASSENGER CONFIGURATION BEGIN
PassengerAppRoot "/home/YOURUSER/KombackWeb"
PassengerBaseURI "/"
PassengerNodejs "/home/YOURUSER/nodevenv/KombackWeb/20/bin/node"
PassengerAppType node
PassengerStartupFile app.js
# DO NOT REMOVE. CLOUDLINUX PASSENGER CONFIGURATION END

# Passenger already routes everything to the Node app, so no SPA fallback is
# needed. If one is ever added for any reason, it must exclude the API and the
# machine-readable endpoints:

# <IfModule mod_rewrite.c>
#   RewriteEngine On
#   RewriteCond %{REQUEST_URI} !^/(api|assets|images)(/|$) [NC]
#   RewriteCond %{REQUEST_URI} !^/(robots\.txt|sitemap\.xml|llms\.txt)$
#   RewriteCond %{REQUEST_FILENAME} !-f
#   RewriteCond %{REQUEST_FILENAME} !-d
#   RewriteRule . /index.html [L]
# </IfModule>

# NEVER do this — it is the cause of the HTML-returned-for-/api bug:
#
#   RewriteRule . /index.html [L]
#   FallbackResource /index.html
#   ErrorDocument 404 /index.html
